        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cymbeline/sceneIII_7.2/p@90899",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "IMOGEN.\nWhy, one that rode to’s execution, man,\nCould never go so slow. I have heard of riding wagers\nWhere horses have been nimbler than the sands\nThat run i’ th’ clock’s behalf. But this is fool’ry.\nGo bid my woman feign a sickness; say\nShe’ll home to her father; and provide me presently\nA riding suit, no costlier than would fit\nA franklin’s huswife.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
